    {
      "id": "f1x1334",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8.2 OOP Concepts"
    },
    {
      "id": "kb5q6yp",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>OOP Concept</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Definition</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Example</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Class</p>",
            "<p>Blueprint/template for creating objects; defines attributes and methods</p>",
            "<p>class Car { String brand; void drive() }</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Object</p>",
            "<p>Instance of a class; has state (attributes) and behaviour (methods)</p>",
            "<p>Car myCar = new Car(); myCar.brand = 'Toyota';</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Encapsulation</p>",
            "<p>Bundle data and methods; hide internal state; access via getters/setters</p>",
            "<p>private int salary; public int getSalary()</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Inheritance</p>",
            "<p>Child class inherits properties and methods from parent class; promotes reuse</p>",
            "<p>class ElectricCar extends Car { int batteryCapacity; }</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Polymorphism</p>",
            "<p>Same interface, different implementations; method overloading and overriding</p>",
            "<p>Animal.sound() — Dog says 'Woof', Cat says 'Meow'</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Abstraction</p>",
            "<p>Hide complex implementation; expose only essential features</p>",
            "<p>abstract class Shape { abstract double area(); }</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Interface</p>",
            "<p>Contract defining what methods a class must implement; no implementation</p>",
            "<p>interface Drawable { void draw(); void resize(); }</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Overloading</p>",
            "<p>Same method name, different parameters in same class (compile-time)</p>",
            "<p>add(int,int) and add(double,double)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Overriding</p>",
            "<p>Child class redefines parent's method (run-time polymorphism)</p>",
            "<p>Dog.sound() overrides Animal.sound()</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "80imvxw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8.3 SOLID Principles"
    },
    {
      "id": "g50g940",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Principle</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Letter</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Meaning</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Violation Example</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Single Responsibility</p>",
            "<p>S</p>",
            "<p>A class should have only one reason to change</p>",
            "<p>Class handles both user data and PDF generation</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Open/Closed</p>",
            "<p>O</p>",
            "<p>Open for extension, closed for modification</p>",
            "<p>If-else chain for each new shape type</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Liskov Substitution</p>",
            "<p>L</p>",
            "<p>Subtypes must be substitutable for base types</p>",
            "<p>Square extends Rectangle but breaks setWidth invariant</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Interface Segregation</p>",
            "<p>I</p>",
            "<p>Don't force clients to implement unused methods</p>",
            "<p>Fat interface with 20 methods; class needs only 2</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Dependency Inversion</p>",
            "<p>D</p>",
            "<p>Depend on abstractions, not concretions</p>",
            "<p>High-level module directly creates low-level MySQL class</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
